  "description": {
   "content": [
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "A simple utility for converting module configurations in fedora.fcfg to Spring bean configuration files.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "This utility should allow conversion of all or a selected part of fedora.fcfg to a Spring bean XML format, akin to the files in $FEDORA_HOME/config/spring/",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "We discussed this utility as part of FCREPO-954, so it could be used by people upgrading from Fedora 3.5...but we think it has general utility beyond just the conversion of DefaultDOManager's configuration to a Spring config file. It could also be used for:",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "1) Plugging in alternative module implementations in Fedora 3.5+, such as utilities that might come out of the Fedora Create community.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "2) A starting point for the eventual conversion of all of fedora.fcfg to Spring configuration files.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    }
   ],
